From: Khovanskiy <a@khovanskiy.ru>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] driver: keep the column type after a NULL value

lua_mysql_push_value marked a NULL value by writing MYSQL_TYPE_NULL
into the field, and the field is shared by all the rows of the result
set. After the first NULL in a column every later value of the column
was read as NULL: 'select 1 union all select null union all select 3'
returned the rows {a = 1}, {} and {} instead of {a = 1}, {} and
{a = 3}, on the plain and on the prepared path alike.

The type of the value is decided locally now, and the field stays as
the server described it.
---
 mysql/driver.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mysql/driver.c b/mysql/driver.c
index ca84296..2c1e450 100755
--- a/mysql/driver.c
+++ b/mysql/driver.c
@@ -198,10 +198,15 @@ lua_mysql_push_value(struct lua_State *L, MYSQL_FIELD *field, void *data,
 	 * Field type isn't MYSQL_TYPE_NULL actually in case of
 	 * Lua's nil passed as value.
 	 * Example: 'conn:execute('SELECT ? AS x', nil)'.
+	 *
+	 * The type is decided here and not written back to the field:
+	 * the field describes the column for every row of the result,
+	 * and a NULL in one row turned all the later values of the
+	 * column into NULL.
 	 */
-	if (data == NULL)
-		field->type = MYSQL_TYPE_NULL;
-	switch (field->type) {
+	enum enum_field_types type = data == NULL ? MYSQL_TYPE_NULL :
+		field->type;
+	switch (type) {
 		case MYSQL_TYPE_TINY:
 		case MYSQL_TYPE_SHORT:
 		case MYSQL_TYPE_LONG:
